1
00:00:00,016 --> 00:00:01,016
[This is a fictional story. All characters
and events bear no relation to reality]

2
00:00:01,016 --> 00:00:02,016
[Child and animal scenes filmed safely]

3
00:00:02,016 --> 00:00:03,616
[under the guardian
and expert supervision per guidelines]

4
00:00:03,616 --> 00:00:07,156
[Episode 13]

5
00:00:07,156 --> 00:00:10,304
Even if it's difficult, make sure
you stretch at home every day.

6
00:00:10,304 --> 00:00:14,172
Take your medication twice a day,
and I'll see you again in a week.

7
00:00:14,172 --> 00:00:15,700
Yes, Doctor. Thank you.

8
00:00:15,700 --> 00:00:17,400
Take care.

9
00:00:20,672 --> 00:00:23,868
Dr. Oh, that was your last patient.

10
00:00:23,868 --> 00:00:25,628
You worked hard today.

11
00:00:25,628 --> 00:00:28,448
Goodness, I didn't realize it was this late.

12
00:00:28,448 --> 00:00:30,749
You did a great job too, Ms. Jung.

13
00:00:32,900 --> 00:00:34,600
Jeez.

14
00:00:42,149 --> 00:00:43,883
[Oh Seong Nam Orthopedic Clinic,
Director Oh Seong Nam]

15
00:00:55,712 --> 00:00:57,952
[Do Not Enter, Investigation in Progress]

16
00:00:58,960 --> 00:01:00,092
Ugh.

17
00:01:00,092 --> 00:01:02,216
They shot him in the eye again.
What's the deal?

18
00:01:02,216 --> 00:01:03,449
Did the bullet just happen to hit his eye?

19
00:01:03,449 --> 00:01:05,200
Or was it intentional?

20
00:01:05,200 --> 00:01:08,144
Twice in a row?
Then it had to be intentional.

21
00:01:08,144 --> 00:01:11,260
Last time, the left eye. Today, the right.

22
00:01:11,260 --> 00:01:13,356
Wow. That's insane.

23
00:01:13,356 --> 00:01:15,744
Why would they do this when they
never even did it to the worst criminals...

24
00:01:15,744 --> 00:01:18,232
Are you sure you found nothing?

25
00:01:18,232 --> 00:01:20,328
Yeah. Nothing again.

26
00:01:20,328 --> 00:01:23,940
At most, he had a traffic fine
for running a light seven years ago.

27
00:01:23,940 --> 00:01:26,604
Anyway, is Kingfisher
seriously insane or what?

28
00:01:26,604 --> 00:01:29,883
Why would he suddenly start killing people
who aren't even criminals?

29
00:01:35,804 --> 00:01:39,896
Wow, it's completely open outside.
Where on earth did the shot come from?

30
00:01:39,896 --> 00:01:42,483
Unless he flew through the air
to take the shot,

31
00:01:43,372 --> 00:01:44,931
he must've fired from across the river.

32
00:01:44,931 --> 00:01:46,508
No way!

33
00:01:46,508 --> 00:01:49,283
From all the way over there?
Is that even possible?

34
00:02:13,960 --> 00:02:17,568
<i>Another shooting has taken place
following last weekend's incident.</i>

35
00:02:17,568 --> 00:02:19,024
[Another Fatal Shooting, Doctor in His 40s]
<i>The latest victim</i>

36
00:02:19,024 --> 00:02:21,144
[Shot Dead in Hospital Office]
<i>was a practicing doctor in his late 40s,</i>

37
00:02:21,144 --> 00:02:24,416
<i>who was killed
late yesterday afternoon in his clinic</i>

38
00:02:24,416 --> 00:02:26,800
[Good Deed Award, Oh Seong Nam]
<i>by a bullet that penetrated the window.</i>

39
00:02:26,800 --> 00:02:28,632
<i>He was pronounced dead at the scene.</i>

40
00:02:28,632 --> 00:02:31,768
<i>Just three days ago, a middle school teacher
in his 50s was shot dead</i>

41
00:02:31,768 --> 00:02:35,516
<i>while crossing a crosswalk
in broad daylight in the heart of the city.</i>

42
00:02:35,516 --> 00:02:38,424
<i>Now, another civilian
has been killed by gunfire,</i>

43
00:02:38,424 --> 00:02:40,860
<i>sending shockwaves across the country.</i>

44
00:02:40,860 --> 00:02:42,280
[Kingfisher Only Targeted Criminals]
<i>As this is the first time Kingfisher,</i>

45
00:02:42,280 --> 00:02:43,948
[Why Kill Innocent Civilians?]
<i>which has only targeted criminals,</i>

46
00:02:43,948 --> 00:02:46,860
[Hero or Murderer?]
<i>has gone after ordinary citizens,</i>

47
00:02:46,860 --> 00:02:48,639
[Public Opinion Turns After Civilian Deaths]
<i>investigators are also looking closely</i>

48
00:02:48,639 --> 00:02:52,540
<i>into the identities of the two victims
and any connection between them.</i>

49
00:02:52,540 --> 00:02:54,349
Who could have...

50
00:03:07,008 --> 00:03:11,392
Honey, I think Yul wants to show
her friends that she went to Jeju Island.

51
00:03:11,392 --> 00:03:12,604
Let's show Daddy.

52
00:03:12,604 --> 00:03:14,304
Ta-da!

53
00:03:15,804 --> 00:03:18,704
Did you have that much fun
going on a trip with Mommy and Daddy?

54
00:03:18,704 --> 00:03:21,916
Yeah, it was so much fun.

55
00:03:21,916 --> 00:03:25,132
Yul, show this to your friends,
and then put it in your bag, okay?

56
00:03:25,132 --> 00:03:26,749
- Okay.
- Okay.

57
00:03:26,749 --> 00:03:29,032
Come on, put it on.

58
00:03:29,032 --> 00:03:32,788
Come on, let's go! Tangerine Girl.

59
00:03:32,788 --> 00:03:34,488
Let's go!

60
00:03:35,883 --> 00:03:37,128
[Seoul Metropolitan Police Agency]

61
00:03:37,128 --> 00:03:40,928
As previously reported,
neither victim had a criminal record,

62
00:03:40,928 --> 00:03:44,383
and no other criminal activity
has been identified.

63
00:03:45,260 --> 00:03:47,476
Is there no connection
between the two victims?

64
00:03:47,476 --> 00:03:51,188
No. At this point, we haven't found
any connection between them.

65
00:03:51,188 --> 00:03:54,576
They have no overlap in hometowns,
schools, occupations, neighborhoods,

66
00:03:54,576 --> 00:03:57,083
or periods of military service.

67
00:03:58,212 --> 00:04:00,516
Have you identified the sniper locations?

68
00:04:01,740 --> 00:04:04,984
The first sniper location was
a building under construction.

69
00:04:04,984 --> 00:04:08,024
There were no CCTV cameras inside,
and the area outside has heavy foot traffic,

70
00:04:08,024 --> 00:04:10,748
making it difficult to identify a suspect.

71
00:04:10,748 --> 00:04:16,096
The second shot was fired from about
two kilometers across the Han River.

72
00:04:16,096 --> 00:04:18,029
Our forensic team
is currently tracking the shooter

73
00:04:18,029 --> 00:04:20,183
based on evidence from the scene.

74
00:04:24,132 --> 00:04:26,792
Isn't it possible that
the shooter isn't Kingfisher?

75
00:04:26,792 --> 00:04:29,216
A copycat, for instance.

76
00:04:35,816 --> 00:04:38,592
Both cases clearly bear similarities
to the previous attacks:

77
00:04:38,592 --> 00:04:43,844
long-range shots, a single bullet,
and the location of the gunshot wound.

78
00:04:43,844 --> 00:04:46,528
But isn't the most important
difference the targets?

79
00:04:46,528 --> 00:04:48,116
In the past 15 years,

80
00:04:48,116 --> 00:04:51,256
Kingfisher has never once
harmed an innocent civilian.

81
00:04:51,256 --> 00:04:53,824
Well, the nature of a crime
can change at any time.

82
00:04:53,824 --> 00:04:56,649
What matters is the method.

83
00:04:58,800 --> 00:05:02,788
Our task force considers Kingfisher
the prime suspect in both cases,

84
00:05:02,788 --> 00:05:04,900
no, in fact, effectively the only suspect,

85
00:05:04,900 --> 00:05:06,849
and we will do everything
we can to apprehend him.

86
00:05:06,849 --> 00:05:07,849
That's all.

87
00:05:07,849 --> 00:05:11,249
[Sniper locations]

88
00:05:22,296 --> 00:05:23,680
Ma'am,

89
00:05:23,680 --> 00:05:27,564
do you have any theory on why
he suddenly changed his targets?

90
00:05:27,564 --> 00:05:29,380
It's extremely rare for a serial killer

91
00:05:29,380 --> 00:05:32,100
like Kingfisher to suddenly
abandon his beliefs.

92
00:05:32,100 --> 00:05:36,383
Especially someone who's followed
such a consistent pattern for so long.

93
00:05:37,612 --> 00:05:40,349
If he's changed his targets, that means...

94
00:05:40,956 --> 00:05:43,683
the purpose behind the killings has changed.

95
00:05:45,552 --> 00:05:49,088
Well, let's wait and see
how the investigation develops.

96
00:05:49,088 --> 00:05:51,149
- Okay.
- Understood.

97
00:05:55,249 --> 00:05:56,592
[Reporter Kwon Tae Seong]

98
00:05:56,592 --> 00:05:58,616
- Oh, one moment, please.
- Yeah.

99
00:06:00,056 --> 00:06:01,756
Where are you?

100
00:06:04,340 --> 00:06:06,220
Doesn't he seem a little down lately?

101
00:06:06,220 --> 00:06:07,661
Kingfisher's someone
he has spent years hunting

102
00:06:07,661 --> 00:06:08,996
in principle as a police officer.

103
00:06:08,996 --> 00:06:12,216
He's spent a long time
studying him in the process.

104
00:06:12,216 --> 00:06:16,249
He couldn't condone it,
but thought the guy drew the line.

105
00:06:17,752 --> 00:06:20,483
Maybe it's a little disillusioning
to see that change?

106
00:06:25,723 --> 00:06:28,028
- What is it?
- A gift from Yul.

107
00:06:28,028 --> 00:06:29,728
A gift?

108
00:06:32,020 --> 00:06:34,188
You went to Jeju Island? When?

109
00:06:34,188 --> 00:06:36,888
Well... Last weekend, with my family.

110
00:06:38,672 --> 00:06:41,100
While some of us are working
our asses off without a single weekend off,

111
00:06:41,100 --> 00:06:43,049
you guys are out having fun.

112
00:06:44,256 --> 00:06:46,400
Yul's gift is so cute.

113
00:06:46,400 --> 00:06:47,444
So...

114
00:06:47,444 --> 00:06:52,052
While we were in Jeju Island,
Seoul was turned completely upside down.

115
00:06:52,052 --> 00:06:54,336
You must've been swamped, huh?

116
00:06:54,336 --> 00:06:58,052
You didn't bring a swamped person here
just to hand over this, right?

117
00:06:58,052 --> 00:07:03,116
You know I can't say anything
beyond the official briefing, right?

118
00:07:06,416 --> 00:07:10,216
Forget the official line.
What's your gut telling you?

119
00:07:12,428 --> 00:07:14,124
Hey.

120
00:07:14,124 --> 00:07:19,056
If there's another punk like Kingfisher
in this country, that's a tragedy.

121
00:07:19,056 --> 00:07:21,083
That's your conclusion?

122
00:07:25,932 --> 00:07:29,820
I think you have a different opinion.

123
00:07:29,820 --> 00:07:32,204
You told me once before.

124
00:07:32,204 --> 00:07:36,020
You said, "Who knows when that gun
might be turned on an innocent person?"

125
00:07:36,020 --> 00:07:38,049
Do you still think that?

126
00:07:39,644 --> 00:07:42,320
What if someone killed them
out of personal revenge

127
00:07:42,320 --> 00:07:45,248
and framed Kingfisher for it?

128
00:07:45,248 --> 00:07:48,549
Is that your conclusion?

129
00:07:50,648 --> 00:07:52,348
Wow.

130
00:07:55,348 --> 00:07:59,596
Why do I feel like
you're defending Kingfisher?

131
00:07:59,596 --> 00:08:02,028
The same punk who threatened you, no less.

132
00:08:02,028 --> 00:08:03,176
If he were the kind of punk
who'd kill anyone,

133
00:08:03,176 --> 00:08:05,916
he would've killed me
instead of threatening me back then.

134
00:08:07,252 --> 00:08:09,600
Got any proof?

135
00:08:09,600 --> 00:08:12,316
Proof that Kingfisher was framed.

136
00:08:14,940 --> 00:08:16,983
That's what I'm going to find out now.

137
00:08:18,312 --> 00:08:21,616
You do your job. I'll do mine.

138
00:08:22,352 --> 00:08:24,052
I'm out.

139
00:08:29,572 --> 00:08:31,149
<i>I knew that punk
would cross the line someday.</i>

140
00:08:31,149 --> 00:08:32,952
<i>He's finally shown his true colors.</i>

141
00:08:32,952 --> 00:08:35,283
<i>A hero who catches criminals?
What a show-off.</i>

142
00:08:35,283 --> 00:08:37,064
- <i>He's the criminal himself.</i>
- <i>True justice?</i>

143
00:08:37,064 --> 00:08:38,752
<i>Catching Kingfisher is justice.</i>

144
00:08:38,752 --> 00:08:40,672
<i>How are we supposed to live like this,
wondering when we'll get shot?</i>

145
00:08:40,672 --> 00:08:42,224
<i>What on earth are the police doing?
Why haven't they caught him yet?</i>

146
00:08:42,224 --> 00:08:44,516
People's views have totally changed.

147
00:08:44,516 --> 00:08:46,166
The comments are all hate too.

148
00:08:46,166 --> 00:08:48,568
These people...

149
00:08:48,568 --> 00:08:50,949
How dare they compare
a fake to the real deal?

150
00:08:52,680 --> 00:08:55,804
Taking someone out with a single shot
from that distance and angle

151
00:08:55,804 --> 00:08:58,349
means he's a professional,
probably on Director Yoo's level.

152
00:08:58,349 --> 00:09:01,483
He's clearly someone who has no qualms

153
00:09:01,483 --> 00:09:05,660
about sacrificing innocent people
to achieve his goal.

154
00:09:05,660 --> 00:09:08,448
What exactly is the point of all this?

155
00:09:08,448 --> 00:09:11,149
Kingfisher's social death?

156
00:09:17,588 --> 00:09:23,283
Instead of attacking me directly,
they're going after public opinion?

157
00:09:25,440 --> 00:09:27,983
If the goal is to turn
Kingfisher into a villain,

158
00:09:27,983 --> 00:09:29,983
two victims won't be enough.

159
00:09:29,983 --> 00:09:32,876
The more victims there are,
the greater the impact.

160
00:09:32,876 --> 00:09:36,283
We have to catch him
before there's a third victim.

161
00:09:36,283 --> 00:09:39,424
Ki Yeong Do,
did you look into what I asked for?

162
00:09:39,424 --> 00:09:41,540
It's ready.

163
00:09:41,540 --> 00:09:43,492
Here's the CCTV footage from the first case.

164
00:09:43,492 --> 00:09:46,716
This was taken just before the shooting.

165
00:09:46,716 --> 00:09:50,736
What's with that disabled man all bundled up?

166
00:09:50,736 --> 00:09:53,276
Isn't he hot in the middle of summer?

167
00:09:53,276 --> 00:09:55,428
Could he be deliberately hiding his face?

168
00:09:55,428 --> 00:09:59,432
Looks like the victim
approached him first to offer help.

169
00:09:59,432 --> 00:10:03,332
The victim had volunteered
with a disability organization before.

170
00:10:03,332 --> 00:10:08,284
He could've used that to lure
the victim to the sniper location.

171
00:10:08,284 --> 00:10:10,292
Your hunch was right.

172
00:10:10,292 --> 00:10:13,904
This is CCTV footage from outside
the hospital that morning.

173
00:10:13,904 --> 00:10:14,904
Oh, look!

174
00:10:14,904 --> 00:10:17,296
There's that man in the wheelchair again.

175
00:10:17,296 --> 00:10:19,032
Why would he go there?

176
00:10:19,032 --> 00:10:21,800
It doesn't look like he had
any particular role that day.

177
00:10:21,800 --> 00:10:23,549
"Catch me if you can."

178
00:10:32,400 --> 00:10:35,249
He's leaving us a trail to follow.

179
00:10:37,649 --> 00:10:39,568
All right. Let's follow it.

180
00:10:39,568 --> 00:10:43,536
Yeah. If we follow it, we'll eventually
find the killer's trail too.

181
00:10:43,536 --> 00:10:46,300
We have to find him
before there's another victim.

182
00:10:46,300 --> 00:10:47,676
You can do it, right?

183
00:10:47,676 --> 00:10:49,616
Yes, understood.

184
00:10:57,216 --> 00:11:00,228
We can't get into the scene.

185
00:11:00,228 --> 00:11:03,548
The hospital's probably closed anyway.

186
00:11:03,548 --> 00:11:05,800
Forget the scene.

187
00:11:05,800 --> 00:11:07,616
Let's start over there.

188
00:11:07,616 --> 00:11:09,332
[Oh Seong Nam Orthopedic Clinic]
Where?

189
00:11:09,332 --> 00:11:13,544
Do you know anything about
Dr. Oh Seong Nam, the director here?

190
00:11:13,544 --> 00:11:14,949
Oh Seong Nam?

191
00:11:14,949 --> 00:11:18,649
I haven't really heard anything about him.

192
00:11:20,444 --> 00:11:22,392
[Oh Seong Nam, Orthopedic Surgeon]

193
00:11:23,768 --> 00:11:25,807
- That's the CCTV camera outside, right?
- Yes.

194
00:11:25,807 --> 00:11:29,492
Can we check three days
of footage around the incident?

195
00:11:29,492 --> 00:11:34,244
Have you noticed anyone suspicious
hanging around here lately?

196
00:11:34,244 --> 00:11:35,944
No.

197
00:11:36,828 --> 00:11:37,828
Here you go.

198
00:11:37,828 --> 00:11:40,916
- We'll make a copy and return it.
- Sure.

199
00:11:40,916 --> 00:11:42,648
[Copying]

200
00:11:42,648 --> 00:11:45,552
Mr. Lee, they found
the second sniper location.

201
00:11:45,552 --> 00:11:47,848
Thank you.

202
00:11:47,848 --> 00:11:48,908
- Let's go.
- Right.

203
00:11:48,908 --> 00:11:50,540
Dr. Oh Seong Nam.

204
00:11:50,540 --> 00:11:52,128
Oh, yes.

205
00:11:52,128 --> 00:11:56,728
Do you happen to remember
anyone who accompanied him?

206
00:11:56,728 --> 00:12:00,516
I'm not sure. Not really.

207
00:12:00,516 --> 00:12:05,312
Oh, I think they were mostly men
around his age.

208
00:12:05,312 --> 00:12:07,349
- Thank you.
- You're welcome.

209
00:12:09,724 --> 00:12:13,568
Were they usually other doctors, then?

210
00:12:13,568 --> 00:12:16,508
Well, I'm not sure about that...

211
00:12:16,508 --> 00:12:17,940
Is this the place?

212
00:12:17,940 --> 00:12:19,864
Yes. Based on the trajectory calculations,

213
00:12:19,864 --> 00:12:22,716
this is the only location
within the margin of error.

214
00:12:28,836 --> 00:12:30,664
The building was completed a few months ago,

215
00:12:30,664 --> 00:12:32,916
but it's still vacant,
so the CCTV wasn't operational.

216
00:12:32,916 --> 00:12:35,916
Wow. I don't know how he
managed to pick a place like this.

217
00:12:43,620 --> 00:12:45,060
Oh, but this is really strange.

218
00:12:45,060 --> 00:12:47,212
What is?

219
00:12:47,212 --> 00:12:49,176
There were no working CCTV cameras
at the first scene either.

220
00:12:49,176 --> 00:12:53,020
Why pick places like this
instead of wiping the footage like before?

221
00:12:53,020 --> 00:12:55,296
Something about this
just doesn't feel like Kingfisher...

222
00:12:55,296 --> 00:12:57,383
And what exactly is "like Kingfisher"?

223
00:12:57,383 --> 00:12:58,852
What?

224
00:12:58,852 --> 00:13:01,300
I mean, starting with the fact
that he's killing innocent people...

225
00:13:01,300 --> 00:13:03,336
Whether he killed guilty people
or innocent people,

226
00:13:03,336 --> 00:13:05,376
he killed someone. We have to catch him.

227
00:13:05,376 --> 00:13:07,444
We just need to do our jobs.

228
00:13:07,444 --> 00:13:09,149
Okay.

229
00:13:10,172 --> 00:13:13,449
We'll know once we catch him
whether he's Kingfisher or not.

230
00:13:16,500 --> 00:13:20,040
Looks like hair was found here too.
There was some over there as well.

231
00:13:20,040 --> 00:13:22,816
Weren't the sniper locations usually clean?

232
00:13:29,856 --> 00:13:34,849
Darn it, who on earth has a death wish?

233
00:13:39,824 --> 00:13:43,896
Darn it, how do I catch this punk?

234
00:13:43,896 --> 00:13:46,949
Just wait till I get my hands on him.

235
00:13:53,728 --> 00:13:55,881
Manager Tae Min,
why are you just sitting there?

236
00:13:55,881 --> 00:13:57,849
You need to do something!

237
00:14:00,920 --> 00:14:03,988
Our Kingfisher is about
to be branded a murderer.

238
00:14:03,988 --> 00:14:05,584
Her reputation is in the gutter!

239
00:14:05,584 --> 00:14:07,188
You two have been friends
since you were kids.

240
00:14:07,188 --> 00:14:09,000
And you're just going to sit there
like it's nothing?

241
00:14:09,000 --> 00:14:12,384
His movement pattern
confirms he was near the crime scene,

242
00:14:12,384 --> 00:14:13,956
though not on the day itself,
but a day or two before.

243
00:14:13,956 --> 00:14:15,668
Oh, what's he saying?

244
00:14:15,668 --> 00:14:18,132
<i>Okay, I'm here.</i>

245
00:14:18,132 --> 00:14:20,424
[Yoo Bo Na]

246
00:14:20,424 --> 00:14:22,052
What are you doing?

247
00:14:22,052 --> 00:14:23,949
Room 1803.

248
00:14:25,888 --> 00:14:28,349
Calm Oh Hyun Nam down.

249
00:14:29,583 --> 00:14:30,783
I'll put the key to good use.

250
00:14:30,783 --> 00:14:32,516
[Yoo Bo Na]

251
00:14:37,448 --> 00:14:39,816
So you were doing something after all.

252
00:14:40,580 --> 00:14:42,383
You really are friends.

253
00:14:44,428 --> 00:14:47,049
But where did Director Yoo go?

254
00:14:48,764 --> 00:14:50,464
Huh?

255
00:15:24,616 --> 00:15:26,900
[Caller ID Restricted]

256
00:15:26,900 --> 00:15:30,332
<i>Surprise! Hi, my friend.</i>

257
00:15:30,332 --> 00:15:32,232
Changed your shoes?

258
00:15:32,232 --> 00:15:35,460
It's too hot to keep wearing those.

259
00:15:35,460 --> 00:15:38,856
Is there anything in the room?
Can you see me?

260
00:15:38,856 --> 00:15:40,308
Why ask?

261
00:15:40,308 --> 00:15:42,592
I know why you came.

262
00:15:42,592 --> 00:15:43,676
But it wasn't me.

263
00:15:43,676 --> 00:15:46,968
I know. The shooting was pretty precise.

264
00:15:46,968 --> 00:15:50,416
You're actually pretty lousy
at sniping, aren't you?

265
00:15:51,632 --> 00:15:53,600
Only because you're a monster.

266
00:15:53,600 --> 00:15:55,716
<i>I'm not exactly lousy, you know.</i>

267
00:15:56,408 --> 00:15:58,568
Did Mama send you?

268
00:15:58,568 --> 00:16:01,249
<i>Mama would be hurt to hear that.</i>

269
00:16:01,976 --> 00:16:03,308
Then who is it?

270
00:16:03,308 --> 00:16:09,480
Someone who can imitate Kingfisher
and wants to bring you down?

271
00:16:09,480 --> 00:16:11,180
<i>I'm busy.</i>

272
00:16:16,876 --> 00:16:19,883
I told you that you'd be the one
to come looking for me first.

273
00:17:16,176 --> 00:17:18,783
Seriously, these monsters...

274
00:17:20,360 --> 00:17:23,696
Yoo Bo Na better watch her back.

275
00:17:23,696 --> 00:17:25,696
[Funeral Hall]
Oh, these people just won't listen.

276
00:17:25,696 --> 00:17:28,060
Get out, seriously!

277
00:17:28,060 --> 00:17:31,796
If you come in here one more time,
I'm calling the police.

278
00:17:31,796 --> 00:17:33,744
Unbelievable, jeez...

279
00:17:33,744 --> 00:17:35,444
Go on in.

280
00:17:38,728 --> 00:17:42,660
In the end, we got kicked out
without even speaking to the family.

281
00:17:42,660 --> 00:17:44,036
At least we paid our respects.

282
00:17:44,036 --> 00:17:46,636
And we got a feel for the atmosphere inside.

283
00:17:46,636 --> 00:17:51,416
What, should we camp out at the entrance too?

284
00:17:55,064 --> 00:17:56,924
<i>They found Kingfisher's
second sniper location.</i>

285
00:17:56,924 --> 00:18:00,600
<i>Head over there. See if you can find
anything at the scene. Anything at all.</i>

286
00:18:00,600 --> 00:18:01,928
That was the Chief.

287
00:18:01,928 --> 00:18:05,056
He wants us to check if they found
anything at the second sniper location.

288
00:18:05,056 --> 00:18:09,908
The reporters camped out there
can cover it themselves.

289
00:18:09,908 --> 00:18:13,708
Let the police handle the shooter.
We'll look into the victims.

290
00:18:13,708 --> 00:18:16,549
Let's check out the first victim tomorrow.

291
00:18:16,549 --> 00:18:17,549
- Okay, sir.
- Well...

292
00:18:17,549 --> 00:18:19,783
He was an upstanding, law-abiding man.

293
00:18:19,783 --> 00:18:22,284
He was kind to his patients.

294
00:18:22,284 --> 00:18:24,624
He must have been
a real family man at home too.

295
00:18:24,624 --> 00:18:26,783
He traveled abroad every year.

296
00:18:26,783 --> 00:18:31,656
He went to Cambodia last year
and was planning to go to Bali this year.

297
00:18:31,656 --> 00:18:35,200
Why would anyone kill a man like that?
That darn Kingfisher.

298
00:18:35,200 --> 00:18:37,316
Jeez, what a punk.

299
00:18:38,948 --> 00:18:41,568
Not long ago they worshiped him as a hero,

300
00:18:41,568 --> 00:18:45,283
and now they treat him
like public enemy number one.

301
00:19:14,749 --> 00:19:16,592
[Tae Seong Chicken]

302
00:19:16,592 --> 00:19:18,292
Ms. Se Ah?

303
00:19:36,949 --> 00:19:38,172
[Seoul Metropolitan Police Agency]

304
00:19:38,172 --> 00:19:40,983
Seoul Metropolitan Police Agency?

305
00:19:41,716 --> 00:19:44,083
[Going All the Way This Time,
Kingfisher Task Force Launched]

306
00:19:44,083 --> 00:19:46,083
[Past Cases Under Review
with New Investigative Techniques]

307
00:19:59,152 --> 00:20:01,364
What is this?

308
00:20:01,364 --> 00:20:02,983
Wait, don't tell me you made this yourself...

309
00:20:02,983 --> 00:20:05,600
No, Sun Il did.

310
00:20:05,600 --> 00:20:08,924
I'm telling you again, I didn't make it.

311
00:20:08,924 --> 00:20:13,249
Sun Il made it to thank you
for boosting sales.

312
00:20:14,156 --> 00:20:15,640
Who cares who made it?

313
00:20:15,640 --> 00:20:18,000
Oh, I was craving something
spicy anyway. This is great.

314
00:20:18,000 --> 00:20:19,472
I'll have to order more often.

315
00:20:19,472 --> 00:20:21,844
You really want to get deep-fried
instead of the chicken, huh?

316
00:20:21,844 --> 00:20:24,704
Why would someone craving
something spicy order chicken?

317
00:20:24,704 --> 00:20:26,340
I nearly died getting all the way here.

318
00:20:26,340 --> 00:20:28,172
Yum!

319
00:20:28,172 --> 00:20:29,188
Is it good?

320
00:20:29,188 --> 00:20:30,888
Yeah.

321
00:20:34,424 --> 00:20:35,564
So...

322
00:20:35,564 --> 00:20:37,852
is police work...

323
00:20:37,852 --> 00:20:40,249
really tough?

324
00:20:41,652 --> 00:20:43,548
Are you worried about me?

325
00:20:43,548 --> 00:20:44,916
Yeah.

326
00:20:44,916 --> 00:20:46,416
As if. You want to die?

327
00:20:46,416 --> 00:20:48,840
Yes or no? Just give me the facts.

328
00:20:48,840 --> 00:20:50,816
"Yes or no? Just give me the facts..."

329
00:20:55,568 --> 00:20:56,768
Huh?

330
00:20:56,768 --> 00:20:58,844
Assistant Manager Ki, what brings you here?

331
00:20:58,844 --> 00:21:02,112
Oh, well, you see.
I wasn't going from here to there.

332
00:21:02,112 --> 00:21:04,776
But I was going from there to here,
and then I saw the convenience store.

333
00:21:04,776 --> 00:21:06,864
I'm really thirsty.
They sell bottled water, right?

334
00:21:06,864 --> 00:21:08,983
Yes, they do. I suppose so.

335
00:21:14,848 --> 00:21:16,949
He came to the convenience store.

336
00:21:25,836 --> 00:21:26,904
Good to see you again.

337
00:21:26,904 --> 00:21:28,604
Indeed.

338
00:21:29,252 --> 00:21:32,883
You seem to really enjoy
butting into other people's business, huh?

339
00:21:33,548 --> 00:21:35,616
But I didn't butt in this time.

340
00:21:39,632 --> 00:21:41,688
You seem to be working yourself to the bone.

341
00:21:41,688 --> 00:21:44,696
Well, do you at least get overtime pay?

342
00:21:44,696 --> 00:21:48,904
Looks like you didn't even wash your hair.
Public service must be taking a toll.

343
00:21:48,904 --> 00:21:51,116
Don't they even let you eat?

344
00:21:51,860 --> 00:21:54,160
I save time by skipping meals.

345
00:21:54,160 --> 00:21:56,204
We're after a very hot target these days.

346
00:21:56,204 --> 00:21:58,336
I hope you're not chasing the wrong shadow.

347
00:21:58,336 --> 00:21:59,608
And who do you think I'm talking about?

348
00:21:59,608 --> 00:22:02,383
The whole world is buzzing about him.

349
00:22:05,384 --> 00:22:07,564
You don't think it's Kingfisher?

350
00:22:07,564 --> 00:22:09,480
Because it's not his style.

351
00:22:09,480 --> 00:22:12,049
Even killers have a style?

352
00:22:13,760 --> 00:22:17,384
Professionally, we call it a "pattern."

353
00:22:17,384 --> 00:22:19,420
A pattern...

354
00:22:19,420 --> 00:22:22,488
Well, the targets have changed.

355
00:22:22,488 --> 00:22:23,756
That's why no message this time.

356
00:22:23,756 --> 00:22:26,360
He copied the method,
but something about it feels different.

357
00:22:26,360 --> 00:22:29,049
So you were thinking the same thing as me?

358
00:22:30,732 --> 00:22:32,860
I never said that.

359
00:22:32,860 --> 00:22:35,084
Your face did.

360
00:22:35,084 --> 00:22:38,849
I'm pretty good at reading people.

361
00:22:42,012 --> 00:22:46,649
Well, sounds like you two
are on the same page.

362
00:22:46,649 --> 00:22:51,296
Now that you're done,
can I make a bombshell announcement?

363
00:22:51,296 --> 00:22:53,820
- A bombshell...
- Announcement?

364
00:22:53,820 --> 00:22:55,520
I'm...

365
00:22:57,176 --> 00:22:58,749
going to become a cop.

366
00:22:58,749 --> 00:23:01,116
I'm going to become a cop.

367
00:23:01,116 --> 00:23:02,188
- What?
- What did you say?

368
00:23:02,188 --> 00:23:05,880
I'm going to become a cop
and catch all the...

369
00:23:05,880 --> 00:23:07,572
- bad guys.
- Wait, why of all things...

370
00:23:07,572 --> 00:23:09,316
Seriously? Awesome!

371
00:23:10,864 --> 00:23:12,229
Is that something to be happy about?

372
00:23:12,229 --> 00:23:14,398
- Then should I try to stop her?
- Of course!

373
00:23:14,398 --> 00:23:16,288
- Why?
- Well...

374
00:23:16,288 --> 00:23:18,764
Because being a cop is dangerous.

375
00:23:18,764 --> 00:23:20,383
Who? The criminals?

376
00:23:20,383 --> 00:23:23,296
And she'd have to study for years
just to pass the exam.

377
00:23:23,296 --> 00:23:25,296
Oh, there's also a special recruitment
program for martial artists.

378
00:23:25,296 --> 00:23:27,140
Really? They have that?

379
00:23:27,140 --> 00:23:28,380
- Look, Se Ah.
- Yes.

380
00:23:28,380 --> 00:23:29,483
- What?
- If you look around,

381
00:23:29,483 --> 00:23:31,384
- you could find...
- I'm rooting for you, Kwon Se Dol!

382
00:23:31,384 --> 00:23:33,020
You know I'll be your senior
if you become a cop, right?

383
00:23:33,020 --> 00:23:34,248
Oh, shut up!

384
00:23:34,248 --> 00:23:36,749
Special recruitment for martial artists?
How does that work?

385
00:23:36,749 --> 00:23:40,132
Here's how you do it.
Well, the competition's pretty stiff.

386
00:23:40,132 --> 00:23:42,552
Having a medal from an international
competition would give you an advantage.

387
00:23:42,552 --> 00:23:43,725
- You don't have one.
- No, but I've won

388
00:23:43,725 --> 00:23:44,749
plenty of domestic competitions.

389
00:23:44,749 --> 00:23:46,162
Really? Then your next shot would be

390
00:23:46,162 --> 00:23:47,816
the Commissioner General's Cup competition...

391
00:23:51,602 --> 00:23:53,820
Oh, this is nice.

392
00:23:56,612 --> 00:23:59,281
What made you make such a drastic decision?

393
00:24:00,020 --> 00:24:01,816
Was it because of your friend?

394
00:24:01,816 --> 00:24:05,716
Oh, well, he did have some influence.

395
00:24:05,716 --> 00:24:11,168
But more than that, I think
being a police officer is a great job.

396
00:24:11,168 --> 00:24:13,916
But why all of a sudden...

397
00:24:15,164 --> 00:24:19,932
It felt like my heart was racing.

398
00:24:19,932 --> 00:24:23,260
When I caught those attackers last time.

399
00:24:23,260 --> 00:24:27,316
And when I caught that
voice phishing scammer recently.

400
00:24:29,852 --> 00:24:35,216
The other day, Assistant Manager Ki,
when you told me you loved me.

401
00:24:35,216 --> 00:24:36,216
Back then, I...

402
00:24:36,216 --> 00:24:38,449
Oh, I know.

403
00:24:38,449 --> 00:24:41,083
You didn't mean anything by it.
You were just saying it casually.

404
00:24:41,083 --> 00:24:46,904
Who'd seriously say that to a woman
they've only met a few times?

405
00:24:46,904 --> 00:24:50,616
That night, I happened to run into Seong Hun.

406
00:24:50,616 --> 00:24:52,510
I asked him to go to a PC bang with me,

407
00:24:52,510 --> 00:24:55,640
but he said he had work
the next day and left.

408
00:24:55,640 --> 00:24:59,772
At first, I found him a bit annoying,
but then it suddenly hit me...

409
00:24:59,772 --> 00:25:02,944
"Oh, I'm this old,

410
00:25:02,944 --> 00:25:07,220
but I don't even
have a job to go to, no career,

411
00:25:07,220 --> 00:25:10,568
and I'm not pulling my weight in society."

412
00:25:10,568 --> 00:25:13,116
Aren't you in grad school?

413
00:25:13,952 --> 00:25:17,604
I just went to grad school
because it was related to my major.

414
00:25:17,604 --> 00:25:20,916
I was wondering
what I should do with my life,

415
00:25:20,916 --> 00:25:24,644
and then I remembered that moment.

416
00:25:24,644 --> 00:25:31,483
How my heart raced
when I caught those bad guys.

417
00:25:33,184 --> 00:25:38,684
I'm not particularly good at anything,
and judo is all I really have.

418
00:25:38,684 --> 00:25:40,404
But if I keep using it,

419
00:25:40,404 --> 00:25:45,883
maybe I can help
make the world a little better?

420
00:25:47,294 --> 00:25:53,032
Se Ah, do you believe the law
and the police can protect everyone?

421
00:25:53,032 --> 00:25:56,976
Unless you're the police,
you can't catch criminals.

422
00:25:56,976 --> 00:25:59,404
And there's no other way
to punish them by law, right?

423
00:25:59,404 --> 00:26:01,204
What if there were another way?

424
00:26:01,204 --> 00:26:04,666
- What?
- Maybe somewhere in this world,

425
00:26:04,666 --> 00:26:07,376
there are people who do that
in a different way.

426
00:26:07,376 --> 00:26:11,033
With the same goal of
making the world a better place,

427
00:26:11,033 --> 00:26:14,128
protecting the people
the police fail to protect,

428
00:26:14,128 --> 00:26:17,216
and punishing those who escape punishment

429
00:26:19,613 --> 00:26:21,313
under the law.

430
00:26:47,223 --> 00:26:53,049
<i>Someone who can imitate Kingfisher
and wants to bring you down?</i>

431
00:27:09,738 --> 00:27:12,668
Yul is finally asleep.
I read her two whole books.

432
00:27:12,668 --> 00:27:15,416
No wonder. I thought you dozed off with her.

433
00:27:15,416 --> 00:27:18,640
Honey, once we finish this,
we're done for the day.

434
00:27:18,640 --> 00:27:21,416
Then shall we have something cold to drink?

435
00:27:22,690 --> 00:27:24,840
How about a beer?

436
00:27:24,840 --> 00:27:26,549
- Beer?
- Yeah.

437
00:27:29,076 --> 00:27:33,332
I heard a beer after putting the kids to bed
tastes like heaven.

438
00:27:33,332 --> 00:27:35,116
- Putting the kids to bed?
- Yeah.

439
00:27:35,879 --> 00:27:36,908
Clocking out of parenting?

440
00:27:36,908 --> 00:27:41,608
So this is what they say washes away
all the day's stress and exhaustion.

441
00:27:41,608 --> 00:27:43,649
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

442
00:27:45,683 --> 00:27:47,683
Oh, that's refreshing.

443
00:27:48,932 --> 00:27:52,716
Oh, it feels like all that
pent-up stress just melts away.

444
00:27:56,949 --> 00:27:59,783
Now I see why people love drinking this.

445
00:28:01,592 --> 00:28:05,849
But you know what? Yul seems
really fascinated by her first plane ride.

446
00:28:05,849 --> 00:28:07,692
She's been talking about it all day.

447
00:28:07,692 --> 00:28:10,136
"Mommy, we flew through the sky, right?"

448
00:28:10,136 --> 00:28:13,108
"The fluffy clouds were
so pretty, weren't they?"

449
00:28:13,108 --> 00:28:15,783
"And we saw the ocean
from up in the sky, too, right?"

450
00:28:15,783 --> 00:28:19,052
Luckily, she wasn't scared of flying at all.

451
00:28:19,052 --> 00:28:21,224
We'll have to take her
on another flight soon.

452
00:28:21,224 --> 00:28:25,644
Yul is pretty... active, you know?

453
00:28:25,644 --> 00:28:26,916
And she's not easily scared.

454
00:28:26,916 --> 00:28:30,580
Maybe she should try something
a little more active, don't you think?

455
00:28:30,580 --> 00:28:32,316
For example, like...

456
00:28:33,752 --> 00:28:35,416
swimming,

457
00:28:36,424 --> 00:28:39,111
taekwondo, or skiing?

458
00:28:39,111 --> 00:28:42,049
Is snowboarding a little wilder than skiing?

459
00:28:42,049 --> 00:28:44,116
She likes scary things.

460
00:28:44,116 --> 00:28:46,283
- What about you?
- Huh?

461
00:28:48,252 --> 00:28:50,649
Don't you have anything you want to do?

462
00:28:52,512 --> 00:28:57,316
I've done everything
I wanted to try since I met you.

463
00:29:00,642 --> 00:29:03,536
Which one did you like best?

464
00:29:03,536 --> 00:29:05,816
I loved them all.

465
00:29:05,816 --> 00:29:07,516
I loved every moment.

466
00:29:10,456 --> 00:29:15,305
Walking hand in hand with you and chatting
as we walked through the flowers.

467
00:29:15,305 --> 00:29:18,483
And all those picnics by the Han River.

468
00:29:18,483 --> 00:29:22,988
And every Sunday, you being the chef
making black bean noodles?

469
00:29:22,988 --> 00:29:27,680
And all those late-night
horror movies you hated.

470
00:29:27,680 --> 00:29:30,708
All the pretty selfies we took together.

471
00:29:30,708 --> 00:29:32,408
All those things.

472
00:29:34,272 --> 00:29:37,283
Well, those are all such ordinary things.

473
00:29:38,016 --> 00:29:40,483
They're all special to me.

474
00:29:41,968 --> 00:29:45,483
There's still so much I want to do with you.

475
00:29:46,604 --> 00:29:48,304
Really?

476
00:29:49,328 --> 00:29:55,949
Something we haven't done before.
Something better and more special.

477
00:29:56,576 --> 00:30:00,780
Let's do every single one of them together.

478
00:30:01,788 --> 00:30:03,624
Yeah.

479
00:30:03,624 --> 00:30:05,416
Together.

480
00:30:08,812 --> 00:30:10,512
Shall we drink?

481
00:30:26,216 --> 00:30:28,649
[Seoul Metropolitan Police Agency]

482
00:30:38,432 --> 00:30:39,783
[Trace Evidence Analysis Report]
Mr. Lee, these are the analysis results

483
00:30:39,783 --> 00:30:41,683
for the trace evidence from the scenes.

484
00:30:43,132 --> 00:30:44,228
No way!

485
00:30:44,228 --> 00:30:45,556
Why? What is it?

486
00:30:45,556 --> 00:30:49,249
They found hair with matching DNA
at both sniper locations?

487
00:30:50,028 --> 00:30:52,776
- What?
- No match in the police database...

488
00:30:52,776 --> 00:30:55,076
But is there any basic profile?
What about the gender?

489
00:30:55,076 --> 00:30:56,624
Oh, here it is!

490
00:30:56,624 --> 00:30:59,883
Female, estimated to be in her 30s?

491
00:31:02,928 --> 00:31:04,880
Wow. What is this?

492
00:31:04,880 --> 00:31:06,580
[Female, Estimated 30s]
If it's a woman...

493
00:31:07,321 --> 00:31:10,116
Could it be the person that pickpocket saw?

494
00:31:13,364 --> 00:31:15,390
We entered the man's build, clothing,

495
00:31:15,390 --> 00:31:16,636
and wheelchair details
into the search program

496
00:31:16,636 --> 00:31:19,440
and tracked his movements
on CCTV over several days.

497
00:31:19,440 --> 00:31:20,964
I found something unusual.

498
00:31:20,964 --> 00:31:22,664
What is it?

499
00:31:23,428 --> 00:31:28,049
He kept going around this area,
so I tracked his movements.

500
00:31:29,268 --> 00:31:31,316
This is what I found.

501
00:31:32,524 --> 00:31:35,552
He went onto that island
and circled its perimeter several times.

502
00:31:35,552 --> 00:31:37,680
I think it might be some kind of message.

503
00:31:37,680 --> 00:31:40,620
The bottom looks like a crescent moon.

504
00:31:40,620 --> 00:31:44,812
The top is the eye,
and the bottom is the eyebrow?

505
00:31:44,812 --> 00:31:46,404
Could it be something like that?

506
00:31:46,404 --> 00:31:49,812
The victims, the eyes.

507
00:31:50,852 --> 00:31:52,704
Oh, you're right.

508
00:31:52,704 --> 00:31:57,284
Both victims were shot in the eye
this time, weren't they?

509
00:31:57,284 --> 00:32:02,668
According to our internal police network,
could this be connected to the case?

510
00:32:02,668 --> 00:32:05,649
The vital spot of every beast

511
00:32:06,472 --> 00:32:08,172
is the eye.

512
00:32:14,840 --> 00:32:20,649
Someone who can imitate Kingfisher
and wants to bring you down?

513
00:32:22,124 --> 00:32:24,840
How long will it take
to trace a restricted number?

514
00:32:24,840 --> 00:32:26,665
If the original number
is still recorded in the network,

515
00:32:26,665 --> 00:32:28,252
it could take as little as 15 minutes.

516
00:32:28,252 --> 00:32:30,183
I need it within ten minutes.

517
00:32:31,976 --> 00:32:33,749
Sooner if possible.

518
00:32:44,788 --> 00:32:46,516
Where are you now?

519
00:33:01,883 --> 00:33:06,749
[Summer 2008, Russia]

520
00:33:19,492 --> 00:33:20,664
The boss is having dinner.

521
00:33:20,664 --> 00:33:22,420
He's having a late dinner, huh?

522
00:33:22,420 --> 00:33:26,968
How can a punk who slaughtered
an entire family stomach his food?

523
00:33:26,968 --> 00:33:28,964
It's a waste of good food.

524
00:33:28,964 --> 00:33:30,516
Let's finish this and go.

525
00:33:30,516 --> 00:33:33,336
Even death row inmates get a last meal.

526
00:33:33,336 --> 00:33:34,524
Just wait.

527
00:33:34,524 --> 00:33:38,249
That's your problem.

528
00:33:39,092 --> 00:33:41,916
If it's too much trouble, I can do it.

529
00:33:42,588 --> 00:33:46,116
A punk like that deserves
a bullet right in the eye...

530
00:33:52,924 --> 00:33:54,648
Haven't seen that before.

531
00:33:54,648 --> 00:33:56,964
Oh, this?

532
00:33:56,964 --> 00:33:59,660
I liked it, so I got one tattooed.

533
00:33:59,660 --> 00:34:01,620
It's just like that saying.

534
00:34:01,620 --> 00:34:04,632
The vital spot of every beast

535
00:34:04,632 --> 00:34:05,876
is the eye.

536
00:34:05,876 --> 00:34:08,416
How is it? Pretty awesome, right?

537
00:34:09,356 --> 00:34:11,283
Keep an eye on the surroundings.

538
00:34:12,183 --> 00:34:13,273
Dinner's over.

539
00:34:13,273 --> 00:34:14,973
He's leaving.

540
00:34:27,908 --> 00:34:29,112
Mission accomplished.

541
00:34:29,112 --> 00:34:30,856
Good work.

542
00:34:30,856 --> 00:34:32,556
Clean up and come back.

543
00:34:42,649 --> 00:34:45,749
Oh, dear. We have a witness.

544
00:34:45,749 --> 00:34:46,783
You must be the boss's daughter.

545
00:34:46,783 --> 00:34:48,883
Layla, wait, let me handle...

546
00:34:58,612 --> 00:35:00,572
Are you insane?

547
00:35:00,572 --> 00:35:02,076
Do you have any idea what you've done?

548
00:35:02,076 --> 00:35:04,608
What? Shot a kid?

549
00:35:04,608 --> 00:35:06,483
Or shot her in the eye?

550
00:35:10,408 --> 00:35:13,796
"Eliminate any witnesses immediately."

551
00:35:13,796 --> 00:35:15,688
I was just following orders.

552
00:35:15,688 --> 00:35:19,216
Isn't the eye a witness's vital spot?

553
00:35:19,888 --> 00:35:22,849
Who on earth gave that kind of order?

554
00:35:23,904 --> 00:35:28,856
"Your name, in death,
only ends up on your tombstone."

555
00:35:28,856 --> 00:35:34,116
"But your sins, even in death,
are passed down to your children."

556
00:35:40,868 --> 00:35:42,449
She was just a child.

557
00:35:42,449 --> 00:35:45,228
She had no weapon and didn't even scream.

558
00:35:45,228 --> 00:35:47,864
She was just a scared little girl.

559
00:35:47,864 --> 00:35:50,376
I heard she was his daughter.

560
00:35:50,376 --> 00:35:52,024
The child was innocent.

561
00:35:52,024 --> 00:35:56,616
Her dad killed countless innocent people.

562
00:35:56,616 --> 00:35:58,283
Some of them were children too.

563
00:35:58,283 --> 00:36:00,649
You used to say it all the time.

564
00:36:00,649 --> 00:36:03,544
I thought you just meant it as a warning.

565
00:36:03,544 --> 00:36:05,548
We've never done anything like this.

566
00:36:05,548 --> 00:36:07,764
Because we'd never been caught.

567
00:36:07,764 --> 00:36:11,360
A witness eventually becomes a voice.

568
00:36:11,360 --> 00:36:13,783
And that voice calls for revenge.

569
00:36:17,000 --> 00:36:19,283
You could've been killed.

570
00:36:21,500 --> 00:36:24,496
Then you should've killed me instead.

571
00:36:24,496 --> 00:36:27,296
"Those children are safe now."

572
00:36:27,296 --> 00:36:29,916
"You saved them."

573
00:36:29,916 --> 00:36:34,472
You said that to me when I was eight.

574
00:36:34,472 --> 00:36:36,568
- I did.
- I don't recall anywhere

575
00:36:36,568 --> 00:36:40,856
in those words saying it's okay
to kill innocent people to save someone.

576
00:36:40,856 --> 00:36:42,556
Is that so?

577
00:36:46,516 --> 00:36:51,296
Today, we broke the most important rule
we're supposed to uphold.

578
00:36:51,296 --> 00:36:53,749
You don't see it the way I do, Mama.

579
00:36:54,400 --> 00:36:56,100
Am I right?

580
00:36:58,592 --> 00:37:00,292
So?

581
00:37:03,576 --> 00:37:08,292
Thank you for raising me
and teaching me all these years.

582
00:37:08,292 --> 00:37:11,583
I thought I'd get the chance
to repay you someday.

583
00:37:17,612 --> 00:37:19,316
Take care of yourself.

584
00:37:29,504 --> 00:37:31,783
You tracked me down faster than I thought.

585
00:37:32,636 --> 00:37:34,916
You already knew.

586
00:37:34,916 --> 00:37:37,616
That's why you came to Korea.

587
00:37:39,724 --> 00:37:41,568
Are you helping her?

588
00:37:41,568 --> 00:37:43,483
Or hunting her?

589
00:37:45,660 --> 00:37:48,216
Losing her every single time?

590
00:37:49,700 --> 00:37:52,483
Seoul is bigger than I thought, isn't it?

591
00:37:53,756 --> 00:37:55,852
What's the reason?

592
00:37:55,852 --> 00:37:58,692
The reason Layla's doing this to me.

593
00:37:58,692 --> 00:38:01,716
In short? Or the long version?

594
00:38:03,188 --> 00:38:05,149
The short version?

595
00:38:08,208 --> 00:38:10,349
Well, resentment toward you?

596
00:38:14,528 --> 00:38:16,383
What do you mean?

597
00:38:16,988 --> 00:38:18,180
Why would she resent me?

598
00:38:18,180 --> 00:38:20,116
Unintentionally,

599
00:38:20,728 --> 00:38:22,983
I happened to see something.

600
00:38:24,184 --> 00:38:26,374
<i>When I heard you two were working together,</i>

601
00:38:26,374 --> 00:38:30,949
<i>I got curious and followed you that day
without you knowing.</i>

602
00:38:34,308 --> 00:38:39,068
<i>She clearly saw that girl,
but why hasn't she told you?</i>

603
00:38:39,068 --> 00:38:41,664
- Mission accomplished.
- Good work.

604
00:38:41,664 --> 00:38:43,364
Clean up and come back.

605
00:38:47,828 --> 00:38:50,336
Oh, dear. We have a witness.

606
00:38:50,336 --> 00:38:53,083
- You must be the boss's daughter.
- Layla, wait, let me handle...

607
00:38:55,472 --> 00:38:57,349
<i>I realized in that moment.</i>

608
00:38:57,349 --> 00:38:59,120
<i>That girl was nothing</i>

609
00:38:59,120 --> 00:39:02,449
- <i>but prey caught in Layla's trap.</i>
- Are you insane?

610
00:39:02,449 --> 00:39:05,180
<i>Layla deliberately let that girl see you.</i>

611
00:39:05,180 --> 00:39:06,880
Take care of yourself.

612
00:39:22,204 --> 00:39:26,884
If you're going to look like you just
lost an arm, you should've stopped her.

613
00:39:26,884 --> 00:39:30,668
She started this life
by her own will and choice.

614
00:39:30,668 --> 00:39:34,416
I promised she could leave
whenever she wanted.

615
00:39:38,356 --> 00:39:40,752
Why didn't you tell her?

616
00:39:40,752 --> 00:39:43,083
That you never gave the order?

617
00:39:44,368 --> 00:39:45,883
Because I wasn't sure.

618
00:39:45,883 --> 00:39:49,488
Because I wasn't sure I could give

619
00:39:49,488 --> 00:39:55,160
the same order
if a witness actually appeared.

620
00:39:55,160 --> 00:39:58,188
A mentor trying to protect her disciple,

621
00:39:58,188 --> 00:40:02,016
and a disciple who'd rather die herself.

622
00:40:04,300 --> 00:40:06,516
It wouldn't have lasted much longer anyway.

623
00:40:08,528 --> 00:40:12,649
Sometimes, she was my mentor too.

624
00:40:14,328 --> 00:40:16,283
Take care of her from now on.

625
00:40:18,088 --> 00:40:19,648
Take care of what?

626
00:40:19,648 --> 00:40:20,832
Yoo Bo Na.

627
00:40:20,832 --> 00:40:23,940
Where she goes, what she does,

628
00:40:23,940 --> 00:40:25,340
and whether she's safe.

629
00:40:25,340 --> 00:40:28,744
Layla was kicked out of
the organization over that.

630
00:40:28,744 --> 00:40:33,808
She moved to Southeast Asia and now
works as a hired killer, quite in demand.

631
00:40:33,808 --> 00:40:37,652
You know what that is, right?
Getting paid to kill people.

632
00:40:37,652 --> 00:40:41,716
Then we recently learned
she'd returned to Korea.

633
00:40:42,764 --> 00:40:44,884
Did Mama send you?

634
00:40:44,884 --> 00:40:47,692
Sorry for being so messed up all this time.

635
00:40:47,692 --> 00:40:51,500
My mom cherishes her disciple
more than her own son,

636
00:40:51,500 --> 00:40:54,408
so can't the son get a little salty about it?

637
00:40:54,408 --> 00:40:56,683
If Kingfisher was the first target,

638
00:40:58,213 --> 00:41:00,312
I must be next.

639
00:41:00,312 --> 00:41:02,416
Well,

640
00:41:02,416 --> 00:41:05,949
do you really think
I don't know what you know?

641
00:41:10,832 --> 00:41:12,749
Your Achilles' heels.

642
00:41:15,692 --> 00:41:18,432
Don't you ever think about coming back?

643
00:41:18,432 --> 00:41:19,992
Mama...

644
00:41:19,992 --> 00:41:22,416
I think she's still waiting for you.

645
00:41:25,168 --> 00:41:27,283
You said you sent her my info.

646
00:41:27,940 --> 00:41:29,912
She probably already knows.

647
00:41:29,912 --> 00:41:32,183
That I'm not coming back.

648
00:41:34,464 --> 00:41:36,249
Give her my regards.

649
00:41:41,352 --> 00:41:43,716
She must be very disappointed.

650
00:41:47,964 --> 00:41:49,632
Did you find her?

651
00:41:49,632 --> 00:41:51,712
No. I'll go myself.

652
00:41:51,712 --> 00:41:53,983
Send me the location.

653
00:42:22,248 --> 00:42:25,704
Ms. Hee Seon, yeah. You're with Yul, right?

654
00:42:25,704 --> 00:42:27,883
Oh, yeah. We just left the daycare.

655
00:42:27,883 --> 00:42:29,332
Did anything seem strange?

656
00:42:29,332 --> 00:42:31,728
Like anyone suspicious hanging around.

657
00:42:31,728 --> 00:42:34,140
No, not at all. Why? Why do you ask?

658
00:42:34,140 --> 00:42:35,544
Oh, it's nothing.

659
00:42:35,544 --> 00:42:39,620
Could you go straight home?
I'm coming to pick her up now.

660
00:42:39,620 --> 00:42:41,783
Okay. Let's go.

661
00:42:42,449 --> 00:42:44,483
[My Heart]

662
00:43:14,008 --> 00:43:15,980
Someone once asked me...

663
00:43:15,980 --> 00:43:17,592
<i>What if...</i>

664
00:43:17,592 --> 00:43:21,616
What would you do if you lost
the things that matter most to you?

665
00:43:22,980 --> 00:43:24,680
I don't know.

666
00:43:25,484 --> 00:43:27,549
I've never thought about it.

667
00:43:28,800 --> 00:43:30,368
Because I don't believe
that will ever happen.

668
00:43:30,368 --> 00:43:35,116
Actually, I sometimes imagine
a life without Tae Seong.

669
00:43:36,576 --> 00:43:40,216
And every time, I can't picture anything.

670
00:43:40,836 --> 00:43:43,116
Just like...

671
00:43:43,116 --> 00:43:45,483
my heart has stopped.

672
00:43:46,168 --> 00:43:47,616
<i>Life without Tae Seong...</i>

673
00:43:47,616 --> 00:43:48,716
[My Heart]

674
00:43:48,716 --> 00:43:51,880
<i>would be like death, right?</i>

675
00:43:51,880 --> 00:43:53,383
<i>Because I love him.</i>

676
00:43:53,383 --> 00:43:54,624
[Big Precious]

677
00:43:54,624 --> 00:43:56,683
<i>Because I love him so much.</i>

678
00:43:56,683 --> 00:43:58,716
[My Heart]

679
00:44:07,513 --> 00:44:08,872
How long has he been inside?

680
00:44:08,872 --> 00:44:11,092
He went in five minutes ago.
He hasn't come out yet.

681
00:44:11,092 --> 00:44:12,792
Really?

682
00:44:27,780 --> 00:44:30,256
Darn it, this punk...

683
00:44:30,256 --> 00:44:31,983
He walked right out.

684
00:44:36,716 --> 00:44:39,683
[Not Today]

685
00:44:39,683 --> 00:44:41,232
[Team Leader Bong]

686
00:44:41,232 --> 00:44:42,424
Yes, Team Leader.

687
00:44:42,424 --> 00:44:45,032
We lost him. The wheelchair was a fake.

688
00:44:45,032 --> 00:44:46,732
What?

689
00:45:21,476 --> 00:45:23,296
Tae Seong!

690
00:45:23,296 --> 00:45:25,798
Honey, what brings you here?

691
00:45:25,798 --> 00:45:27,205
Why weren't you answering your phone?

692
00:45:27,205 --> 00:45:28,723
- I called you several times.
- My phone?

693
00:45:28,723 --> 00:45:31,916
I must've left it at the office.
Sorry, but what's up? Is something wrong?

694
00:45:31,916 --> 00:45:33,852
No, nothing's wrong.

695
00:45:33,852 --> 00:45:36,556
Well, actually... It's just that, honey.

696
00:45:36,556 --> 00:45:40,483
Someone I know said they were sending me
a package, so I gave them an address.

697
00:45:40,483 --> 00:45:43,404
Then I realized I'd stupidly
given them your office address.

698
00:45:43,404 --> 00:45:44,796
You did?

699
00:45:44,796 --> 00:45:47,083
So I called you a few times,
but you didn't answer.

700
00:45:47,083 --> 00:45:49,734
So I was passing by and thought
I'd stop in and see you.

701
00:45:49,734 --> 00:45:51,380
- Sorry to bother you while you're busy.
- No, it's fine.

702
00:45:51,380 --> 00:45:52,424
You came out to get it?

703
00:45:52,424 --> 00:45:54,328
Of course, I did. It's totally fine.

704
00:45:54,328 --> 00:45:55,912
- Sorry.
- It's fine. Don't worry.

705
00:45:55,912 --> 00:45:58,394
- I should get back to work.
- Okay.

706
00:45:58,394 --> 00:46:00,483
- Take care.
- Bye!

707
00:46:04,252 --> 00:46:05,283
- Honey.
- Yeah?

708
00:46:05,283 --> 00:46:07,216
Why does it feel so hard to leave?

709
00:46:07,820 --> 00:46:09,280
Are you working late tonight?

710
00:46:09,280 --> 00:46:10,778
I have some outside work,
but it should end early.

711
00:46:10,778 --> 00:46:12,449
I'll come home early.

712
00:46:13,760 --> 00:46:17,549
Okay. See you at home.
I really should go, as much as I hate to.

713
00:47:09,112 --> 00:47:13,652
<i>Your name, in death,
only ends up on your tombstone.</i>

714
00:47:13,652 --> 00:47:19,012
<i>But your sins, even in death,
are passed down to your children.</i>

715
00:47:19,012 --> 00:47:21,183
<i>Layla, wait, let me handle...</i>

716
00:47:26,416 --> 00:47:29,488
[Ms. Hee Seon]

717
00:47:29,488 --> 00:47:31,883
Yeah, Ms. Hee Seon, are you home now?

718
00:47:31,883 --> 00:47:33,468
You're with Yul, right?

719
00:47:33,468 --> 00:47:35,296
Bo Na, I can't find Yul anywhere!

720
00:47:35,296 --> 00:47:37,108
<i>What should I do?</i>

721
00:47:37,108 --> 00:47:38,292
As reported earlier,

722
00:47:38,292 --> 00:47:41,800
hair with matching DNA was found
at both sniper locations.

723
00:47:41,800 --> 00:47:46,516
The NFS analysis indicates
it belongs to a woman in her 30s.

724
00:47:57,736 --> 00:47:59,788
Please zoom in there.

725
00:47:59,788 --> 00:48:01,304
<i>Accordingly, we narrowed the suspect pool</i>

726
00:48:01,304 --> 00:48:02,904
[Suspect Pool Narrowed Down]
to women in their 30s.

727
00:48:02,904 --> 00:48:07,220
After rechecking CCTV and dashcam footage
collected around the crime scenes,

728
00:48:07,220 --> 00:48:11,316
we found one woman
who was present at both scenes.

729
00:48:11,316 --> 00:48:12,764
Is she really the same person?

730
00:48:12,764 --> 00:48:15,116
Her clothes and shoes are all different.

731
00:48:19,892 --> 00:48:24,464
As you can see, she has
the same tattoo in the same spot.

732
00:48:24,464 --> 00:48:27,144
A crescent moon below and an eye above.

733
00:48:27,144 --> 00:48:31,483
As you know, both victims
were shot in the eye.

734
00:48:32,500 --> 00:48:36,032
A dashcam from a car parked near
the second crime scene captured this woman

735
00:48:36,032 --> 00:48:38,949
[A Woman Gets in a Car and Drives Off]
getting into a car and driving off.

736
00:48:38,949 --> 00:48:40,540
[Zoom in on License Plate]
We ran the plate,

737
00:48:40,540 --> 00:48:41,899
[Owner: A Man in His 70s]
and the owner turned out to be a man

738
00:48:41,899 --> 00:48:43,328
[Who Died Three Years Ago]
in his 70s who died three years ago.

739
00:48:43,328 --> 00:48:45,112
So it's a stolen-identity car.

740
00:48:45,112 --> 00:48:46,256
Well, that's undeniable proof.

741
00:48:46,256 --> 00:48:47,968
[Seoul Traffic Control Center]
<i>We're using every available resource</i>

742
00:48:47,968 --> 00:48:50,104
<i>to track down the vehicle,
including the AI-powered integrated system</i>

743
00:48:50,104 --> 00:48:53,200
<i>for searching wanted vehicles
and intelligent CCTV systems</i>

744
00:48:53,200 --> 00:48:55,716
<i>operated by local governments.</i>

745
00:49:07,635 --> 00:49:09,335
Ugh.

746
00:49:13,632 --> 00:49:16,449
<i>It's been delivered.</i>

747
00:49:39,740 --> 00:49:41,144
Please spare me.

748
00:49:41,144 --> 00:49:43,048
Please, spare my life.

749
00:49:43,048 --> 00:49:47,552
If you want to live,
tell me what I want to hear.

750
00:49:47,552 --> 00:49:50,020
Oh... I really don't know anything.

751
00:49:50,020 --> 00:49:53,516
I've never even seen them.
I just did what I was paid to do.

752
00:49:56,672 --> 00:49:58,372
Unlock it.

753
00:50:19,624 --> 00:50:21,416
- Please let me see it.
- You can't.

754
00:50:21,416 --> 00:50:22,776
Bo Na, you're here?

755
00:50:22,776 --> 00:50:24,920
The kids wanted some, so we came.

756
00:50:24,920 --> 00:50:26,400
And while I was paying for a second...

757
00:50:26,400 --> 00:50:27,583
I asked to see the CCTV inside,

758
00:50:27,583 --> 00:50:28,928
[Authorized Personnel Only]
but they said no.

759
00:50:28,928 --> 00:50:32,560
Well, I told you I can't
just show it to anyone.

760
00:50:32,560 --> 00:50:35,204
If it's that important, bring the police.

761
00:50:35,204 --> 00:50:36,712
Excuse me.

762
00:50:36,712 --> 00:50:38,412
Hey!

763
00:50:43,652 --> 00:50:45,436
Oh, my. Who is that woman?

764
00:50:45,436 --> 00:50:48,249
Bo Na, do you know her?

765
00:51:01,328 --> 00:51:06,968
<i>Lately, I sometimes sense
something strange around me.</i>

766
00:51:06,968 --> 00:51:12,683
<i>Every time, every cell in
my body goes on high alert.</i>

767
00:51:13,524 --> 00:51:16,568
<i>I get this feeling that some danger</i>

768
00:51:16,568 --> 00:51:20,549
<i>stemming from me
could reach my child, my husband,</i>

769
00:51:21,320 --> 00:51:23,696
my family...

770
00:51:23,696 --> 00:51:25,416
Anxiety.

771
00:51:29,140 --> 00:51:33,483
<i>And every time, I pray with all my heart.</i>

772
00:51:34,440 --> 00:51:36,683
<i>If the blade cannot be stopped,</i>

773
00:51:37,320 --> 00:51:39,588
<i>let it come to me.</i>

774
00:51:39,588 --> 00:51:43,484
<i>Let the gun aim only at me.</i>

775
00:51:43,484 --> 00:51:45,184
Yul!

776
00:51:56,224 --> 00:51:58,083
Oh, Yul!

777
00:52:10,184 --> 00:52:11,436
Kwon Yul!

778
00:52:11,436 --> 00:52:12,740
Huh? Mommy!

779
00:52:12,740 --> 00:52:14,844
Lady, my mommy is here!

780
00:52:14,844 --> 00:52:16,852
Huh?

781
00:52:16,852 --> 00:52:18,840
Where did she go?

782
00:52:18,840 --> 00:52:20,448
Who?

783
00:52:20,448 --> 00:52:21,644
Yul, who was here?

784
00:52:21,644 --> 00:52:23,836
- Huh?
- Yeah, your friend.

785
00:52:23,836 --> 00:52:24,964
My friend?

786
00:52:24,964 --> 00:52:28,060
Yeah. She was pushing me
on the swing just now.

787
00:52:28,060 --> 00:52:30,016
But where did she go?

788
00:52:40,068 --> 00:52:44,216
Yul, I told you not
to follow strangers, remember?

789
00:52:44,216 --> 00:52:47,168
How could you come here alone
without telling Ms. Hee Seon?

790
00:52:47,168 --> 00:52:50,040
She's not a stranger. She's your friend.

791
00:52:50,040 --> 00:52:52,049
How do you know she's my friend?

792
00:52:52,049 --> 00:52:54,180
I've never shown you my friends.

793
00:52:54,180 --> 00:52:56,760
She showed me a photo of you two.

794
00:52:56,760 --> 00:52:58,460
A picture?

795
00:52:59,940 --> 00:53:01,983
Mommy, see? It's her.

796
00:53:06,336 --> 00:53:11,032
<i>"The vital spot of every beast is the eye."</i>

797
00:53:11,032 --> 00:53:12,952
<i>How is it? Pretty awesome, right?</i>

798
00:53:12,952 --> 00:53:17,104
<i>Enough playing around. Hurry over.</i>

799
00:53:17,104 --> 00:53:18,883
<i>I miss you.</i>

800
00:53:19,900 --> 00:53:22,152
As I mentioned on the phone,

801
00:53:22,152 --> 00:53:27,384
he was a teacher who was
respected his whole life.

802
00:53:27,384 --> 00:53:28,536
- I see.
- Yeah.

803
00:53:28,536 --> 00:53:33,416
Even now, his former students
still visit him on Teachers' Day.

804
00:53:38,792 --> 00:53:44,268
That was taken when he went to
Cambodia last summer.

805
00:53:44,268 --> 00:53:45,700
Cambodia?

806
00:53:45,700 --> 00:53:47,383
That's Angkor Wat in the background.

807
00:53:47,383 --> 00:53:50,580
It was one of his bucket-list trips.

808
00:53:50,580 --> 00:53:56,449
He went to Cambodia last year
and was planning to go to Bali this year.

809
00:54:02,140 --> 00:54:03,840
Hello.

810
00:54:05,316 --> 00:54:08,849
You remember me, right?
We met at the restaurant the other day.

811
00:54:09,664 --> 00:54:11,049
Oh, yes.

812
00:54:11,049 --> 00:54:16,016
It's just that you seemed to
have something to tell me that day.

813
00:54:16,016 --> 00:54:19,916
Could you tell me now, if that's okay?

814
00:54:27,383 --> 00:54:29,988
They came to the restaurant together.
Both of them.

815
00:54:29,988 --> 00:54:35,144
By both, you mean the doctor and...

816
00:54:35,144 --> 00:54:38,249
The middle school teacher who was shot first.

817
00:54:46,620 --> 00:54:48,872
Not just long-range.
Get me something for close range too.

818
00:54:48,872 --> 00:54:50,852
A suppressor, a knife, and a flashlight too.

819
00:54:50,852 --> 00:54:52,508
Hurry.

820
00:54:52,508 --> 00:54:54,576
Found it!

821
00:54:54,576 --> 00:54:58,704
The vehicle is currently
at the Yanghwa Han River Park parking lot.

822
00:54:58,704 --> 00:55:00,976
Finally!

823
00:55:00,976 --> 00:55:02,584
Get ready to move out.

824
00:55:02,584 --> 00:55:04,284
Yes, sir!

825
00:55:10,504 --> 00:55:12,560
Huh? Yul, Daddy's home!

826
00:55:12,560 --> 00:55:14,816
- I'm home.
- Daddy!

827
00:55:14,816 --> 00:55:17,249
Yul! There you are!

828
00:55:17,249 --> 00:55:18,552
You're home?

829
00:55:18,552 --> 00:55:20,480
What brings you here? Where is Bo Na?

830
00:55:20,480 --> 00:55:24,252
She had something urgent come up,
so she asked me to watch Yul.

831
00:55:24,252 --> 00:55:25,292
Something urgent? What happened?

832
00:55:25,292 --> 00:55:28,949
Well, I don't know either.
Must be something at work.

833
00:56:15,216 --> 00:56:17,416
Hi, my friend.

834
00:56:19,548 --> 00:56:21,076
Oh...

835
00:56:21,076 --> 00:56:24,064
Should I greet you the Korean way here?

836
00:56:24,064 --> 00:56:26,940
It's been a while, Yoo Bo Na.

837
00:56:26,940 --> 00:56:29,096
Why did you kill those people?

838
00:56:29,096 --> 00:56:31,024
What?

839
00:56:31,024 --> 00:56:34,596
That's the first thing you ask
before we've even caught up?

840
00:56:34,596 --> 00:56:38,916
Because I need to decide whether to kill you.

841
00:56:40,016 --> 00:56:41,584
Right.

842
00:56:41,584 --> 00:56:44,020
Our noble Kingfisher

843
00:56:44,020 --> 00:56:47,848
isn't the type to kill just anyone
over a bad mood.

844
00:56:47,848 --> 00:56:49,749
Should I wait longer?

845
00:56:50,416 --> 00:56:52,612
Sorry to disappoint you.

846
00:56:52,612 --> 00:56:55,049
That won't be enough to kill me.

847
00:56:57,684 --> 00:57:01,483
Did you know grilled bananas
taste like roasted sweet potatoes?

848
00:57:04,000 --> 00:57:06,372
There was a woman who always asked

849
00:57:06,372 --> 00:57:10,036
if I'd eaten whenever I came back from a job.

850
00:57:10,036 --> 00:57:12,764
She was a woman selling
cheap food on the street.

851
00:57:12,764 --> 00:57:15,783
No matter how often I ignored her,
she'd ask every day.

852
00:57:17,504 --> 00:57:19,483
"Have you eaten?"

853
00:57:20,148 --> 00:57:22,464
She wasn't afraid of anything.

854
00:57:22,464 --> 00:57:25,516
To someone who'd just
come back from killing someone...

855
00:57:27,064 --> 00:57:31,483
One day, I was hungry,
so I stopped and looked.

856
00:57:31,483 --> 00:57:35,916
She gathered up some food
and had her little daughter bring it to me.

857
00:57:37,368 --> 00:57:42,508
From then on, grilled bananas
from that woman became my dinner.

858
00:57:42,508 --> 00:57:44,649
One day, the mom and daughter

859
00:57:45,432 --> 00:57:49,008
were found dead in a pile of trash.

860
00:57:49,008 --> 00:57:53,449
It took me a while to find out who did it.

861
00:57:54,956 --> 00:57:58,083
I wondered whether to gouge out their eyes

862
00:57:58,083 --> 00:58:00,449
or tear them apart.

863
00:58:01,449 --> 00:58:05,984
While having fun pondering that,
I thought this way was pretty good too.

864
00:58:05,984 --> 00:58:10,316
Kill the ones who deserve it
and bring down Kingfisher too.

865
00:58:11,588 --> 00:58:13,288
Bang!

866
00:58:14,840 --> 00:58:17,656
Why are you doing this to me?

867
00:58:17,656 --> 00:58:20,560
I don't think I've done anything to you.

868
00:58:20,560 --> 00:58:22,283
Because you annoy me.

869
00:58:23,632 --> 00:58:27,383
Seeing you living like that
while I live like this,

870
00:58:28,176 --> 00:58:30,249
it makes my stomach churn.

871
00:58:34,349 --> 00:58:39,012
I killed that girl to protect Yoo Bo Na.

872
00:58:39,012 --> 00:58:43,249
I thought that's what you wanted,
Mama. Was I wrong?

873
00:58:44,044 --> 00:58:46,696
You should've killed Yoo Bo Na instead.

874
00:58:46,696 --> 00:58:48,396
What do you mean...

875
00:58:51,183 --> 00:58:56,528
Yoo Bo Na said,
"You should've killed me instead."

876
00:58:56,528 --> 00:58:58,316
Do you understand what that means?

877
00:59:00,544 --> 00:59:03,383
Not really.

878
00:59:04,568 --> 00:59:08,464
You don't know what Yoo Bo Na knows.

879
00:59:08,464 --> 00:59:10,632
That's why.

880
00:59:10,632 --> 00:59:12,416
That's why I'm casting you out.

881
00:59:12,416 --> 00:59:15,472
You're... kicking me out?

882
00:59:15,472 --> 00:59:16,828
Why?

883
00:59:16,828 --> 00:59:18,468
I... I...

884
00:59:18,468 --> 00:59:21,649
A girl who could kill without batting an eye.

885
00:59:21,649 --> 00:59:23,728
I was worried, but I kept watching.

886
00:59:23,728 --> 00:59:27,283
Sometimes, that nature
can be useful in the field.

887
00:59:27,283 --> 00:59:32,752
But you shouldn't have crossed the line.

888
00:59:32,752 --> 00:59:36,716
You shouldn't have proven
what kind of person you are.

889
00:59:36,716 --> 00:59:40,649
I wanted to be family.

890
00:59:41,888 --> 00:59:47,683
But no matter how hard I tried,
you only looked at Bo Na.

891
00:59:48,344 --> 00:59:50,604
How are we so different?

892
00:59:50,604 --> 00:59:52,816
She kills people, and so do I!

893
00:59:52,816 --> 00:59:54,900
It's just a fine line.

894
00:59:54,900 --> 00:59:57,200
Separated by a single fine line.

895
00:59:57,200 --> 01:00:02,044
How big a difference
that fine line makes will be proven

896
01:00:02,044 --> 01:00:05,483
by how your lives turn out.

897
01:00:06,204 --> 01:00:07,983
Don't you agree?

898
01:00:08,784 --> 01:00:12,580
<i>I should have killed you back then
instead of that girl.</i>

899
01:00:12,580 --> 01:00:16,808
That's how I was abandoned,
and this is how I live now.

900
01:00:16,808 --> 01:00:18,508
Thanks to you.

901
01:00:20,280 --> 01:00:21,980
No.

902
01:00:23,204 --> 01:00:26,249
You're the one who made you who you are.

903
01:00:28,136 --> 01:00:30,864
If you got what you wanted,
now go home quietly.

904
01:00:30,864 --> 01:00:32,900
While you're still alive.

905
01:00:32,900 --> 01:00:35,083
It's too late for that.

906
01:00:35,780 --> 01:00:39,683
I figured you'd be living
more or less like me.

907
01:00:40,328 --> 01:00:42,820
- <i>But...</i>
- Kingfisher,

908
01:00:42,820 --> 01:00:44,676
isn't he honestly amazing?

909
01:00:44,676 --> 01:00:46,040
He really is!

910
01:00:46,040 --> 01:00:47,840
The world needs someone like that.

911
01:00:47,840 --> 01:00:51,048
I wonder what he's like. I'm so curious.

912
01:00:51,048 --> 01:00:52,720
I'd love to meet him.

913
01:00:52,720 --> 01:00:56,348
<i>People here revere you like a hero?</i>

914
01:00:56,348 --> 01:01:00,583
While over there, everyone treats me
like a criminal punk.

915
01:01:02,152 --> 01:01:03,916
Mommy, are we staying the night?

916
01:01:03,916 --> 01:01:05,649
Yeah, we're staying one night.

917
01:01:05,649 --> 01:01:06,683
Yay!

918
01:01:06,683 --> 01:01:10,449
<i>You've got a loving husband,
a beautiful daughter, and...</i>

919
01:01:11,692 --> 01:01:13,852
<i>you even have a family.</i>

920
01:01:13,852 --> 01:01:16,583
<i>You even look pretty happy.</i>

921
01:01:22,964 --> 01:01:24,883
It's not fair.

922
01:01:26,388 --> 01:01:27,812
What we do...

923
01:01:27,812 --> 01:01:30,136
isn't all that different.

924
01:01:30,136 --> 01:01:31,836
You and I

925
01:01:32,668 --> 01:01:35,268
are going to hell when we die.

926
01:01:35,268 --> 01:01:37,649
The same hell?

927
01:01:38,440 --> 01:01:39,800
That sounds somewhat fair.

928
01:01:39,800 --> 01:01:42,083
I'll take my fair share of punishment.

929
01:01:42,872 --> 01:01:45,752
If there's punishment
I have to face while I'm alive,

930
01:01:45,752 --> 01:01:47,516
I'll take that too.

931
01:01:48,332 --> 01:01:50,032
But...

932
01:01:51,300 --> 01:01:53,083
leave my family out of this.

933
01:01:54,076 --> 01:01:56,216
I'm warning you.

934
01:01:56,216 --> 01:02:00,800
If you lay a finger on
my husband or my child,

935
01:02:00,800 --> 01:02:03,584
I'll make you experience hell
while you're still alive.

936
01:02:03,584 --> 01:02:05,668
Is that so?

937
01:02:05,668 --> 01:02:08,416
Then you can experience hell
while you're alive too.

938
01:02:09,676 --> 01:02:13,052
Get destroyed just like me.

939
01:02:13,052 --> 01:02:15,749
Forget everything you hold dear.

940
01:03:36,584 --> 01:03:39,464
Try killing me in front of your husband.

941
01:03:39,464 --> 01:03:41,283
It's you, Layla.

942
01:03:41,283 --> 01:03:42,283
Let's get her.

943
01:03:42,283 --> 01:03:44,536
The suspect must be taken alive.

944
01:03:44,536 --> 01:03:48,224
Yoo Bo Na, enjoy rotting in prison
for the rest of your life.

945
01:03:48,224 --> 01:03:50,160
Dong Jin's here. We have to go.

946
01:03:50,160 --> 01:03:51,540
We have to go. Hurry.

947
01:03:51,540 --> 01:03:54,244
I'll become your living hell.

948
01:03:54,244 --> 01:03:55,296
Ceasefire!

949
01:03:55,296 --> 01:03:59,449
Without you... how am I supposed to live?

950
01:04:00,949 --> 01:04:02,649
[Mommy, I miss you. I love you so much]
